Release Notes - v1.1.0

## General

- Ticket status values are no longer restricted to "open" and "closed".

## CLI

- Added `get`, `set`, and `clear` commands for general ticket metadata.
- Added a `description` command to extract complete, short, or detailed ticket descriptions.
- Added atomic updates for multiple metadata items in one command.
- Added dated history entries when an existing status changes.
- Added `--no-comment` to suppress status history entries.
- Removed the `close` and `reopen` commands. Use `set <id> status:<value>` instead.

## Visual Studio Code:

- Added configurable ticket groups that map to status values.
- Added user and workspace settings for status groups.
- Added a configurable initial status for new tickets.
- Added a permanent Uncategorized group for missing and unmapped statuses.
- Replaced Close and Reopen actions with a general Set Status action.
- Added ticket counters to status groups.
- Added support for multiple ticket folders in one project.
- Added folder-based ticket grouping and folder selection when creating tickets.

